Menu="Utilities"
Title="ZFS Master NG"
Icon="zfs.master.png"
Tag="zfs.master.png"
---
<?php
$plugin = "zfs.master";

require_once "$docroot/plugins/$plugin/include/ZFSMHelpers.php";
require_once "$docroot/plugins/$plugin/include/ZFSMReplicaServe.php";
require_once "$docroot/plugins/$plugin/include/ZFSMReplicaRemote.php";

$zfsm_cfg = loadConfig(parse_plugin_cfg($plugin, true));
$zfsm_version = zfsmPluginVersion("/var/log/plugins/$plugin.plg");

?>
   
<link type="text/css" rel="stylesheet" href="<?php autov('/plugins/zfs.master/styles/zfsm-forms.css'); ?>">
<?php if ($zfsm_version !== ''): ?><p class="zfsm-version"><?=zfsmHtml(_('Version').' '.$zfsm_version)?></p><?php endif; ?>

<form markdown="1" name="<?=$plugin?>_settings" method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame">
<input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="<?=zfsmHtml($var['csrf_token'] ?? '')?>"/>
<input type="hidden" name="#file" value="zfs.master/zfs.master.cfg"/>
<input type="hidden" name="#section" value="general"/>
<input type="hidden" name="#command" value="plugins/zfs.master/scripts/alerts.php"/>
<input type="hidden" name="#arg[1]" value="schedule"/>
<details class="zfsm-section" open markdown="1">
<summary>_(General Settings)_</summary>

_(Refresh Interval)_:
: <select id="refresh_interval" name="refresh_interval" size="1">
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['refresh_interval'], "0", _('No refresh'))?>
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['refresh_interval'], "30", _('30 seconds'))?>
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['refresh_interval'], "60", _('1 Minute'))?>
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['refresh_interval'], "120", _('2 Minutes'))?>
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['refresh_interval'], "300", _('5 Minutes'))?>
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['refresh_interval'], "900", _('15 Minutes'))?>
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['refresh_interval'], "1800", _('30 Minutes'))?>
  </select>

:zc_settings_refresh_interval_plug:
> How often the Main tab reloads pools, datasets and snapshots. It pauses while the tab is in the background.
> Choose **No refresh** to reload only when you click the refresh button or an action succeeds.
:end


_(Lazy Load)_:
: <select name="lazy_load">
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['lazy_load'], "0", _('No'))?>
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['lazy_load'], "1", _('Yes'))?>
  </select>

:zc_settings_lazy_load_plug:
> **Yes** shows datasets straight away, then fills in snapshots one pool at a time.
> Use it when a pool with many snapshots makes the Main tab slow to appear.
:end

_(Load ZnapZend Data)_:
: <select name="znapzend_data">
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['znapzend_data'], "0", _('No'))?>
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['znapzend_data'], "1", _('Yes'))?>
  </select>
  
:zc_settings_znapzend_data_plug:
> **Yes** reads the ZnapZend backup plans stored on each dataset and shows them in its details.
> Leave it on **No** if you don't use ZnapZend.
:end

_(Size Units)_:
: <select name="size_units">
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['size_units'], "binary", _('ZFS (GiB)'))?>
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['size_units'], "decimal", _('Unraid (GB)'))?>
  </select>

:zc_settings_size_units_plug:
> **ZFS** shows sizes in powers of 1024 (GiB, TiB), the units zfs and zpool print.
> **Unraid** shows them in powers of 1000 (GB, TB), rounded as Unraid's Main page does, so the same pool reads the same in both tables.
> Either way a pool's Size, Used and Free are its usable space, as in Unraid's pool tables; zpool's raw total shows only while the pool's top dataset can't be read.
:end


_(Destructive Mode)_:
: <select name="destructive_mode">
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['destructive_mode'], "0", _('No'))?>
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['destructive_mode'], "1", _('Yes'))?>
  </select>
  
:zc_settings_destructive_mode_plug:
> **Yes** adds Rename, Edit and Destroy to dataset menus, and Convert and Delete to folder menus.
> It also lets a rollback remove newer snapshots, and a snapshot delete include child datasets. Each action still asks first.
:end

_(Debug Log)_:
: <select name="debug_log">
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['debug_log'], "0", _('No'))?>
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['debug_log'], "1", _('Yes'))?>
  </select>

:zc_settings_debug_log_plug:
> **Yes** also writes the commands the plugin runs, with how each ended and its time, and the name of each request to its admin page, to a log of their own, `/var/log/zfs.master.debug.log`. A replication, a rewrite and a receive stream their commands and log their own lines in `/var/log/zfs.master.log` whether this is on or not; the rsync that copies a folder into a dataset, and a diagnostics run's own commands, are in neither. Each log never passes about 1 MB, so its oldest lines go first; a diagnostics zip holds both.
> Turn it on to reproduce a problem, make the zip, then turn it off again. rsync's arguments, and those of a command that names where a key is kept, are left out.
:end


</details>

<details class="zfsm-section" open markdown="1">
<summary>_(Datasets)_</summary>

_(Datasets Exclusion Patterns (Just One!))_:
: <textarea name="exclusion" cols="40" rows="1" placeholder="/dockerfiles/.*"><?=zfsmHtml($zfsm_cfg['dataset_exclusion'])?></textarea> <span id="zfsm-exclusion-warning" style="color:#e22828"></span>

:zc_settings_datasets_exclusion_plug:
> Hides datasets whose names match this regular expression, with their child datasets, snapshots and any matching folders. Matching ignores case, except in a pattern with `%`.
> For example `/docker` hides every dataset with /docker in its name. A `.` matches any character, so write `\.` for a dot. A pattern with `%` is read as a Lua pattern, the format older versions used; there a dot is `%.`.
:end

_(Directory Listing (Dataset names, one per line!))_:
: <textarea name="directory_listing" cols="40" rows="10" placeholder="mypool/docker&#10;mypool/otherdataset"><?=zfsmHtml(implode(PHP_EOL, $zfsm_cfg['directory_listing']))?></textarea>

:zc_settings_directory_listing_plug:
> One dataset name per line, such as `cache/appdata`. The Main tab then lists the folders directly inside each one.
:end


</details>

<details class="zfsm-section" open markdown="1">
<summary>_(Snapshots)_</summary>

_(Dataset Icon Alert Max Days)_:
: <input type="text" name="snap_max_days_alert" value="<?=$zfsm_cfg['snap_max_days_alert']?>">

:zc_settings_dataset_icon_color_plug:
> Days since a dataset's last snapshot before its camera icon turns orange. Datasets with no snapshots stay grey.
:end

_(Snapshots Pattern)_:
: <input type="text" name="snap_pattern" value="<?=zfsmHtml($zfsm_cfg['snap_pattern'])?>" placeholder="default Y-m-d-His">

:zc_settings_snapshots_pattern_plug:
> Date format for snapshots taken from the Main tab, written with [PHP date letters](https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.date.php).
> `Y-m-d-His` gives names like `tank/data@2026-11-03-181920`.
:end

_(Snapshot Time)_:
: <select name="snap_utc">
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['snap_utc'], "0", _('Local time'))?>
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['snap_utc'], "1", _('UTC'))?>
  </select>

:zc_settings_snapshots_utc_plug:
> The clock used for the date in new snapshot names. UTC names sort the same on every server and across daylight-saving changes.
:end

_(Snapshots Prefix (Do not include the '@'))_:
: <input type="text" name="snap_prefix" value="<?=zfsmHtml($zfsm_cfg['snap_prefix'])?>" placeholder="default blank">

:zc_settings_snapshots_prefix_plug:
> Text placed before the date in new snapshot names. Leave out `@`.
> With `zfs-master-`, names look like `tank/data@zfs-master-2026-11-03-181920`.
:end

</details>

<details class="zfsm-section" open markdown="1">
<summary>_(Alerts)_</summary>

_(Pool Health Alerts)_:
: <select name="alert_interval">
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['alert_interval'], "0", _('Off'))?>
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['alert_interval'], "15", _('Every 15 minutes'))?>
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['alert_interval'], "60", _('Hourly'))?>
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['alert_interval'], "1440", _('Daily'))?>
  </select>

:zc_settings_alerts_interval_plug:
> Sends an Unraid notification when a pool is not ONLINE, has read, write or checksum errors or damaged files, or is still not imported 10 minutes after the array starts; and again when it recovers.
> Checks start once the array has started. With **Off**, ZFS is read only while the Main tab is open.
:end

_(Stale Snapshot Alerts)_:
: <select name="alert_stale">
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['alert_stale'], "0", _('Off'))?>
	<?=mk_option($zfsm_cfg['alert_stale'], "1", _('On'))?>
  </select>

:zc_settings_alerts_stale_plug:
> With pool health alerts on, also notifies when a dataset's newest snapshot is older than **Dataset Icon Alert Max Days**.
> Datasets with no snapshots, and datasets the exclusion pattern hides, are left out.
:end

</details>

<details class="zfsm-section" open markdown="1">
<summary>_(Replication)_</summary>

_(Accept Replicas Into)_:
: <input type="text" name="replica_accept" value="<?=zfsmHtml($zfsm_cfg['replica_accept'])?>" placeholder="off"> <span id="zfsm-replica-accept-warning" style="color:#e22828"></span>

:zc_settings_replica_accept_plug:
> Other servers running ZFS Master NG may replicate into this dataset, each into its own dataset inside it, which never mounts or shows as a block device, with setuid, devices and exec off. Leave it empty to accept none; a pool's top dataset isn't accepted.
> Add a sender's key under Users, root, SSH authorized keys as one line starting `restrict,from="<its address>",command="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zfs.master/scripts/replica-serve.php <its name>"`. That key can then only list, check and receive copies inside this dataset's `<its name>`: it can't destroy, roll back or replace anything, or run anything else. Paste exactly that one line: any other line there is a key with no limits.
> `from=` takes the sender's exact IP addresses, separated by commas when it has more than one: no ranges, wildcards, `!` or host names.
> A quota on this dataset caps the space all copies use. This server's SSH host key is `<?=zfsmHtml(zfsmHostKeyFingerprint() ?? 'unreadable')?>`; compare it with the one a sender shows before it trusts this server.
:end

_(Sender Keys)_:
: <span id="zfsm-replica-keys"><?=zfsmReplicaKeysHtml(zfsmReplicaKeys())?></span>

:zc_settings_replica_keys_plug:
> The keys in root's authorized_keys that run replica-serve.php. Each one's line must hold restrict (with no limit turned back on after it), a from= of exact IP addresses, and command= exactly the script and its sender's name; one in red does not.
:end

</details>

&nbsp;
: <input type="submit" name="#apply" value="_(Apply)_" disabled><input type="button" value="_(Done)_" onclick="done()">
</form>

<details class="zfsm-section" open markdown="1">
<summary>_(Replicate To Other Servers)_</summary>

_(This Server's Key)_:
: <span id="zfsm-send-key"><?=zfsmReplicaKeyHtml()?></span> <span id="zfsm-send-key-status" style="color:#e22828"></span>

:zc_settings_send_key_plug:
> This server's own SSH key for sending copies, made here once. Its private half is kept on the flash drive, unencrypted: keep the flash share and every flash backup private. A server added below accepts copies from it once its own Settings name a dataset under **Accept Replicas Into** and its root adds the line shown under it to SSH authorized keys (Users, root).
:end

_(Servers)_:
: <span id="zfsm-send-servers"><?=zfsmReplicaRemotesHtml(zfsmReplicaRemotes())?></span> <span id="zfsm-send-servers-status" style="color:#e22828"></span>

:zc_settings_send_servers_plug:
> The servers this one may send copies to, each with the host key read when it was added. A server whose host key changes is refused until it is removed and added again. Test makes this server's dataset there if it is missing, and shows its name.
> The line's `from=` is the address this server reaches that server from. Where a router between them changes that address (source NAT), that server sees another one and refuses the key: set `from=` there to the exact address it sees.
:end

_(Add A Server)_:
: <input type="text" id="zfsm-send-name" placeholder="name" aria-label="Name" style="width:8em"> <input type="text" id="zfsm-send-host" placeholder="IP address" aria-label="IP address"> <input type="text" id="zfsm-send-port" value="22" aria-label="SSH port" style="width:4em"> <input type="button" value="Read Host Key" onclick="zfsmSendScan()"> <span id="zfsm-send-found" aria-live="polite"></span>

:zc_settings_send_add_plug:
> The name is how this list shows the server. Compare the host key read here with the one that server's ZFS Master NG Settings show under Accept Replicas Into; tick that they match, then Add.
:end

</details>

<details class="zfsm-section" open markdown="1">
<summary>_(Diagnostics)_</summary>

_(Unraid Diagnostics)_:
: <input type="checkbox" id="zfsm-diag-unraid" checked>

:zc_settings_diag_unraid_plug:
> Put Unraid's own diagnostics zip inside the plugin's. It goes in as Unraid made it: this plugin changes nothing in it, and its system log can name datasets.
:end

_(Diagnostics Zip)_:
: <input type="button" id="zfsm-diag-start" value="_(Generate)_"> <span id="zfsm-diag-status"></span><a id="zfsm-diag-link" href="#" style="display:none"></a>

:zc_settings_diag_zip_plug:
> Collects what a bug report needs into one zip: the plugin's settings, install and log, the pools and datasets as it reads them, what this browser shows, and what it finds wrong. The zip is kept in `/boot/logs`, the newest three of them.
> Dataset, snapshot and folder names, addresses and keys are replaced by tokens before anything is packed; pool names stay.
> If this page does not load, run `/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zfs.master/scripts/diagnostics.php` in a terminal: it prints what it finds and the zip's path.
:end

</details>

<script src="<?php autov('/plugins/zfs.master/frontend/ZFSMDiagnostics.js'); ?>"></script>
<script>
var zfsm_tips = <?=zfsmJson(array(
	'refresh_interval' => _('How often the Main tab reloads pool and dataset details.'),
	'lazy_load' => _('Show datasets first, then load snapshots one pool at a time.'),
	'znapzend_data' => _('Show ZnapZend backup plans on each dataset.'),
	'size_units' => _('Show sizes in ZFS units (GiB) or Unraid units (GB).'),
	'destructive_mode' => _('Show rename, edit and destroy, and allow deletes of folders and newer snapshots.'),
	'debug_log' => _('Also write the commands the plugin runs, and the requests it gets, to a debug log.'),
	'exclusion' => _('Hide datasets and listed folders whose names match this pattern.'),
	'directory_listing' => _('Datasets whose folders are listed on the Main tab, one per line.'),
	'snap_max_days_alert' => _('Days since the last snapshot before the camera icon turns orange.'),
	'snap_pattern' => _('Date format for new snapshot names, using PHP date() letters.'),
	'snap_prefix' => _('Text placed before the date in new snapshot names.'),
	'snap_utc' => _('Clock used for the date in new snapshot names.'),
	'alert_interval' => _('How often to check pool health and send Unraid notifications.'),
	'alert_stale' => _('Also notify when snapshots are older than the Max Days setting.'),
	'replica_accept' => _('The dataset other servers may replicate into. Empty accepts none.'),
), JSON_HEX_TAG | JSON_HEX_AMP)?>;
$('details.zfsm-section dl').each(function() {
	var name = $(this).find('[name]').attr('name');
	if (zfsm_tips[name]) $(this).children('dt').addClass('zfsm-tip').attr({'data-tip': zfsm_tips[name], tabindex: 0});
});
$('textarea[name="exclusion"]').on('change', function() {
	$.post('/plugins/zfs.master/backend/ZFSMAdmin.php', {cmd: 'validateexclusion', pattern: $(this).val()}, function(answer) {
		$('#zfsm-exclusion-warning').text(answer.valid ? '' : 'This pattern is invalid and would be ignored.');
	}, 'json');
});
// Checked on load too, without a change event, so the saved value shows its warning and Apply stays off.
function zfsmCheckAccept(value) {
	if (value === '') return $('#zfsm-replica-accept-warning').text('');
	$.post('/plugins/zfs.master/backend/ZFSMAdmin.php', {cmd: 'validateaccept', dataset: value}, function(answer) {
		$('#zfsm-replica-accept-warning').text(answer.valid ? '' : 'Not a dataset inside a pool, so nothing is accepted.');
	}, 'json');
}
$('input[name="replica_accept"]').on('change', function() { zfsmCheckAccept($(this).val()); });
zfsmCheckAccept($('input[name="replica_accept"]').val());

// Outside the form, so its tick box never arms Apply. A run already going, or the last zip, shows on load.
var zfsm_diagnostics = createZFSMDiagnostics({url: '/plugins/zfs.master/backend/ZFSMAdmin.php', download: '/plugins/zfs.master/backend/ZFSMDiagDownload.php?file=',
	button: $('#zfsm-diag-start'), box: $('#zfsm-diag-unraid'), status: $('#zfsm-diag-status'), link: $('#zfsm-diag-link'), report: function() { return zfsmDiagReport(window); }});
$('#zfsm-diag-start').on('click', zfsm_diagnostics.start);
zfsm_diagnostics.poll();
window.addEventListener('pagehide', zfsm_diagnostics.stop);
// A page brought back from the browser's cache asks again: what it showed was stopped when it was left.
window.addEventListener('pageshow', function(event) { if (event.persisted) zfsm_diagnostics.poll(); });

// Replicate To Other Servers: each answer carries what its action gives (the refreshed HTML, a host key and its fingerprint,
// or the area a test found) or, as error, why not. Unraid's page adds the token to every post ($.ajaxPrefilter, DefaultPageLayout.php).
var zfsm_send_found = null;
var zfsm_send_asked = 0;
function zfsmSendPost(data, done) {
	$.post('/plugins/zfs.master/backend/ZFSMAdmin.php', data, function(answer) {
		answer = answer || {};
		// ZFSMAdmin's catch-all answers {failed: {request: why}}, with no error.
		if (!answer.error && answer.failed) answer = {error: Object.values(answer.failed)[0] || 'The request failed'};
		done(answer);
	}, 'json').fail(function() { done({error: 'No answer from this server'}); });
}
function zfsmSendKey() {
	// Off while it runs: a second click would answer "already has its key" beside the new key.
	var button = $('#zfsm-send-key input[type=button]').prop('disabled', true);
	zfsmSendPost({cmd: 'replicakey'}, function(answer) {
		$('#zfsm-send-key-status').text(answer.error || '');
		if (answer.error) return button.prop('disabled', false);
		$('#zfsm-send-key').html(answer.key_html);
		$('#zfsm-send-servers').html(answer.servers_html);
	});
}
function zfsmSendScan() {
	var asked = {host: $('#zfsm-send-host').val(), port: $('#zfsm-send-port').val()};
	var found = $('#zfsm-send-found').css('color', '').text('Reading…');
	var ask = ++zfsm_send_asked;
	zfsm_send_found = null;
	zfsmSendPost($.extend({cmd: 'replicascan'}, asked), function(answer) {
		// An answer for an address or port changed since is dropped.
		if (ask !== zfsm_send_asked) return;
		if (answer.error) return found.css('color', '#e22828').text(answer.error);
		zfsm_send_found = $.extend(asked, {key: answer.key, fingerprint: answer.fingerprint});
		var add = $('<input type="button" value="Add" disabled>').on('click', zfsmSendAdd);
		var match = $('<input type="checkbox">').on('change', function() { add.prop('disabled', !this.checked); });
		found.empty().append(document.createTextNode('Host key '+answer.fingerprint+' '), $('<label>').append(match, ' matches that server\'s Settings'), ' ', add);
	});
}
// A changed address or port needs its own host key read again.
$('#zfsm-send-host, #zfsm-send-port').on('input', function() { zfsm_send_asked++; zfsm_send_found = null; $('#zfsm-send-found').empty(); });
function zfsmSendAdd() {
	if (!zfsm_send_found) return;
	var ask = zfsm_send_asked;
	var found = $('#zfsm-send-found');
	found.children('.zfsm-send-refused').remove();
	// Off while it runs: a second click would answer "already a server here" for an Add that worked.
	var controls = found.find('input').prop('disabled', true);
	zfsmSendPost($.extend({cmd: 'replicaadd', name: $('#zfsm-send-name').val()}, zfsm_send_found), function(answer) {
		if (!answer.error) $('#zfsm-send-servers').html(answer.servers_html);
		// A host key read since keeps its fields and its Add.
		if (ask !== zfsm_send_asked) return;
		if (answer.error) {
			// Add and its ticked box come back: a name put right is added without reading the host key again.
			controls.prop('disabled', false);
			return found.append($('<span class="zfsm-send-refused" style="color:#e22828">').text(' '+answer.error));
		}
		zfsm_send_found = null;
		found.empty();
		$('#zfsm-send-name, #zfsm-send-host').val('');
	});
}
function zfsmSendRemove(name) {
	zfsmSendPost({cmd: 'replicaremove', name: name}, function(answer) {
		$('#zfsm-send-servers-status').text(answer.error || '');
		if (!answer.error) $('#zfsm-send-servers').html(answer.servers_html);
	});
}
function zfsmSendTest(name, id) {
	var status = $(document.getElementById(id)).css('color', '').text('Asking…');
	zfsmSendPost({cmd: 'replicatest', name: name}, function(answer) {
		if (answer.error) return status.css('color', '#e22828').text(answer.error);
		status.text('Ready: copies go into '+answer.area);
	});
}
</script>
